{"kind": "melee", "attachment": [1, 1, 0], "findings": [{"level": "error", "title": "The model is facing the wrong way", "body": "A melee should fit within 10x10x35, and yours (3x14x2) would if it were turned. Use the rotate buttons under 'Turn it' - weapons point forward along the long axis, hats point up.", "voxels": []}, {"level": "error", "title": "2 voxels are almost black", "body": "Trove's style guide asks for nothing darker than (10, 10, 10) - pure black reads as a hole in game. Use a dark grey instead.", "voxels": [4, 36]}, {"level": "warning", "title": "3 voxels are not connected to the model", "body": "These only touch the rest of the model at a corner, or not at all. Trove renders them, but the style guide asks for face-connected geometry.", "voxels": [1, 2, 36]}, {"level": "warning", "title": "The handle sits too high or too low", "body": "There shouldn't be more than 5 voxels above or 4 below the attachment point; yours has 12 above and 1 below.", "voxels": []}, {"level": "warning", "title": "The grip is crowded", "body": "Around the attachment point there should be nothing in a 3x3x3 cube except the handle running lengthwise - that space is the hand.", "voxels": [0, 1, 2, 5, 6, 7]}], "satisfied": ["A blueprint stores one material per voxel, so alpha-on-solid and specular-on-glass - two of the classic .qb mistakes - can't happen here.", "Attachment point recorded at (1, 1, 0)."], "counts": {"error": 2, "warning": 3, "info": 0}}